    "user": "U08EXEA8V2R",
    "text": "About lab10, it seems that `pci_set_dma_mask` and `pci_set_consistent_dma_mask` don't exist in v6.12.6\n\u003chttps://elixir.bootlin.com/linux/v5.17.15/A/ident/pci_set_consistent_dma_mask\u003e\nBased on this random driver, I'm guessing they were merged in 5.18 into `dma_set_mask_and_coherent`\n\u003chttps://elixir.bootlin.com/linux/v5.17.15/source/drivers/fpga/dfl-pci.c#L358\u003e\n\u003chttps://elixir.bootlin.com/linux/v5.18/source/drivers/fpga/dfl-pci.c#L358\u003e\n\nThe issue is in the lab\n\u003chttps://students.mimuw.edu.pl/ZSO/PUBLIC-SO/2024-2025/10_pci/index-en.html#lab-pci-en\u003e\nand in adlerdev.c\n```51d50\n\u0026lt;       .owner = THIS_MODULE,\n262,264c261\n\u0026lt;       if ((err = pci_set_dma_mask(pdev, DMA_BIT_MASK(32))))\n\u0026lt;               goto out_mask;\n\u0026lt;       if ((err = pci_set_consistent_dma_mask(pdev, DMA_BIT_MASK(32))))\n---\n\u0026gt;       if ((err = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(\u0026amp;pdev-\u0026gt;dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(32))))```\nAlso, adlerdev qemu does not compile without `./configure --disable-libnfs --disable-werror` and `CFLAGS=-Wno-int-conversion` on most recent systems",
    "ts": "1747750591.241659",
    "team": "TV7BVTSJK",
